    <p class="av-tldr"><b>TLDR: Mëva gives you 180mg of magnesium in two berry gummies, with the dose printed big on the front and only the UK-authorised claims.</b> 👇</p>

    <h2>1. The Dose Is Printed on the Front, Not Hidden on the Back</h2>
    <img class="av-img" src="{{ 'meva-ad-A4-feed.jpg' | file_img_url: '900x' }}" alt="Jar of Mëva with the dose circled in red: 180mg magnesium, 2 a day" loading="eager">
    <p>Tired of turning a bottle round and squinting at tiny print, trying to work out how much magnesium you&#39;re actually getting?</p>
    <p>On a lot of labels, the big number on the front isn&#39;t the magnesium itself. It&#39;s the whole compound. <b>The amount of magnesium is often somewhere on the back, in small type.</b></p>
    <p>Mëva prints it on the front, big enough to read from the kettle: <b>180mg magnesium · 2 a day.</b> That&#39;s 48% of your daily reference intake, and nothing to decode.</p>

    <h2>2. For the Afternoons That Run on Empty</h2>
    <img class="av-img" src="{{ 'meva-g3-02.jpg' | file_img_url: '900x' }}" alt="What magnesium does: the authorised claims" loading="lazy">
    <p>3pm. Kettle on again. The to-do list hasn&#39;t got any shorter, and neither has the queue of people who need something from you.</p>
    <p>Here&#39;s what UK law allows us to say about magnesium, word for word: <b>magnesium contributes to a reduction of tiredness and fatigue.</b> It also contributes to normal psychological function and to normal muscle function.</p>
    <p>No miracle language. No promises we can&#39;t back. Just the authorised claims, and two gummies a day.</p>
    <p class="av-src">source: GB Nutrition and Health Claims Register, authorised claims for magnesium.</p>

    <h2>3. Your Plate Might Not Be Covering It</h2>
    <img class="av-img" src="{{ 'meva-g3-05.jpg' | file_img_url: '900x' }}" alt="What&#39;s inside a Mëva gummy" loading="lazy">
    <p>You eat well most days. But busy days, skipped lunches and one more coffee instead of a proper meal add up quietly.</p>
    <p>The UK&#39;s own national diet survey found that the average woman gets <b>about 83% of her recommended magnesium from food</b>, and <b>15% of women aged 19 to 64 don&#39;t reach even the minimum.</b></p>
    <p>Two Mëva gummies add 180mg a day. The gap, covered, without overhauling your diet.</p>
    <p class="av-src">source: National Diet and Nutrition Survey 2019&ndash;2023, OHID &amp; Food Standards Agency, 2025.</p>

    <h2>4. One Form, Named on the Label: Magnesium Citrate</h2>
    <img class="av-img" src="{{ 'meva-g3-04.jpg' | file_img_url: '900x' }}" alt="Glossy magenta Mëva gummy with blackberries" loading="lazy">
    <p>Some magnesium products mix three or four forms into one big total, so you never know how much of each you&#39;re getting.</p>
    <p>Mëva uses <b>one form, magnesium citrate</b>, with the exact amount on the label: 90mg in every gummy. Nothing hidden in a blend.</p>

    <h2>5. A Supplement You&#39;ll Actually Remember to Take</h2>
    <img class="av-img" src="{{ 'meva-g3-06b.jpg' | file_img_url: '900x' }}" alt="Two Mëva gummies compared with a handful of tablets" loading="lazy">
    <p>Be honest: how many half-finished tubs of tablets are in your cupboard right now?</p>
    <p>A supplement only works if you take it. Mëva is a <b>ripe red berry gummy</b>: soft, glossy, no water, no swallowing. Four seconds by the kettle and you&#39;re done.</p>
    <p><b>It&#39;s not just the tablets you&#39;re tired of. It&#39;s one more chore.</b></p>
    <p>Vegan, gelatine-free, made without the 14 major allergens. And yes, it&#39;s a gummy, so it contains sugar: the full ingredients list is on our product page.</p>

    <h2>6. Women Are Already Joining the No Drama Club</h2>
    <div class="av-grid">{%- for i in (1..4) -%}<img src="{{ 'meva-studio-' | append: i | append: '.jpg' | file_img_url: '400x' }}" alt="" loading="lazy">{%- endfor -%}</div>
    <p class="av-cap">From our No Drama Club campaign shoot. Pictured: models.</p>
    <p>We launch in January, and women across the UK are already saving their spot in the Founding 500. When they join, we ask one optional question: <i>&ldquo;What&#39;s draining you most right now?&rdquo;</i></p>
    <div class="av-rev"><b>The answer we hear most</b><p class="big">&ldquo;Not feeling like me.&rdquo;</p><p>Followed by: <b>&ldquo;Carrying everyone.&rdquo;</b></p><small>Real, anonymous answers from the waitlist form. These are not product reviews: reviews open when the first jars arrive.</small></div>

    <h2>7. Join the Founding 500 and Try It With Our First-Jar Guarantee</h2>
    <img class="av-img" src="{{ 'meva-studio-3.jpg' | file_img_url: '900x' }}" alt="Woman holding a jar of Mëva and a gummy" loading="lazy">
    <p>Founding 500 members get <b>20% off a single jar</b> on their first order, <b>free UK delivery on 2+ jars</b>, and first dibs on our small first batch. Nothing to pay today.</p>
    <p>Give it a proper go: two gummies a day for a full jar.</p>
    <p><b>Finish your first jar. Not for you? We&#39;ll refund it.</b> Claim within 45 days of delivery. First order only, one per household.</p>

